---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Question from '../components/Question.astro';
import { getApps, hasPage, statusLabel } from '../lib/apps';

const apps = (await getApps()).filter(hasPage);
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Accessibility · Niko"
  description="How Niko apps are built and tested for accessibility, and how to report a problem."
>
  <header class="hero">
    <h1>Accessibility</h1>
    <p class="lead">Niko apps are made for people mainstream apps leave out.</p>
  </header>

  <main id="main">
    <section aria-labelledby="built">
      <h2 id="built">How we build</h2>
      <ul class="promise">
        <li><strong>Spoken.</strong> Apps speak in the phone's own voice and language, so they can be used without reading.</li>
        <li><strong>Labelled.</strong> Every button and setting has a TalkBack label.</li>
        <li><strong>Large.</strong> Big touch targets, and text that follows the phone's font size up to 200%.</li>
        <li><strong>High contrast.</strong> 7:1 contrast in light and dark themes.</li>
        <li><strong>Calm.</strong> The main screen never scrolls or moves around.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="tested">
      <h2 id="tested">How we test</h2>
      <p>Android's accessibility checks run on every build. Before an app reaches version 1.0 it also gets a full TalkBack pass, checks at 200% font size, an Accessibility Scanner pass, a native speaker review of each language, and everyday use by the people it is made for.</p>
      <p>Each app's page says how far it has got:</p>
      <ul class="links">
        {apps.map((app) => (
          <li><a href={`/${app.id}/#accessibility`}>{app.data.name}</a>: {statusLabel[app.data.status].toLowerCase()}, version {app.data.version}</li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="faq">
      <h2 id="faq">Questions</h2>

      <Question q="Can someone who can't read use Niko apps?">
        <p>Yes, that is who they are made for. The main action of each app is spoken out loud, and a helper can do the setup.</p>
      </Question>

      <Question q="Do they work with TalkBack?">
        <p>Every button and setting has a label. A full TalkBack pass of every screen happens before version 1.0, and the app's page says if it hasn't happened yet.</p>
      </Question>

      <Question q="Which languages do they speak?">
        <p>It differs by app. Each app's page lists the languages it speaks and the languages its screens are in. If the phone has no voice for a language, the app says so instead of speaking another one.</p>
      </Question>

      <Question q="Do Niko apps meet WCAG or another standard?">
        <p>We don't claim conformance with any standard until an app has been fully tested. This website meets WCAG AAA contrast.</p>
      </Question>

      <Question q="Can I help test?">
        <p>Yes, especially with someone who would use the app every day. See <a href="/about/#help">how to help</a>.</p>
      </Question>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="report">
      <h2 id="report">Tell us what doesn't work</h2>
      <p>If something is hard to use, we want to know. Email <a href="mailto:hello@gopalkhadka.com.np">hello@gopalkhadka.com.np</a> or open an issue on the app's GitHub page. A voice message or a few words is enough.</p>
      <p class="status">Last updated 18 October 2026.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
